  {
    "name": "azure_run",
    "description": "Execute synchronous JavaScript in a retained QuickJS context. Azure host calls wait internally and return ordinary values; promises and async functions are unsupported. Use az.graph for fleet inventory, az.request for reviewed ARM routes, az.metrics.single({cloud, resourceId, metricNames, timespan?, interval?, aggregation?, top?, orderBy?, filter?, resultType?, metricNamespace?, autoAdjustTimegrain?, validateDimensions?, rollupBy?}) for one resource, az.metrics.batch({cloud, region, resourceIds, metricNamespace, metricNames, startTime?, endTime?, interval?, aggregation?, top?, orderBy?, filter?, rollupBy?}) for up to 50 same-type resources, and az.logs.query({cloud, subscription?, workspaceId, query, timespan}) for explicitly granted Log Analytics KQL. Cloud is never inferred from `az cloud set`: pass exactly `AzureCloud` for commercial Azure or `AzureUSGovernment` for US Government on every helper call. For example, replace the zero-GUID placeholder in az.logs.query({cloud: \"AzureUSGovernment\", workspaceId: \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\", query: \"AppRequests | take 10\", timespan: \"PT1H\"}). workspaceId is the Log Analytics Workspace ID GUID, exposed as `properties.customerId` on a `Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces` resource; it is not the workspace name or ARM resource ID, and it is not an Application Insights appId. When starting from an Application Insights component, use az.graph to follow its `properties.WorkspaceResourceId` to the workspace, then use that workspace resource's `properties.customerId`. Metrics batch also requires an explicit regional endpoint. With localCapabilities: [\"artifacts.write\"], az.artifacts.writeJson({name, value}) creates one compact JSON file up to 480 KiB. For larger iterable results, use az.artifacts.writeJsonArray({name, values, compression?}) for a top-level JSON array or az.artifacts.writeJsonLines({name, values, compression?}) for JSON Lines; compression may be \"lz4\", filenames must end in .json/.jsonl with an additional .lz4 suffix when compressed, and logical output is bounded at 64 MiB. All artifact helpers return a private local receipt. Oversized serializable results expose a context-scoped ref envelope; use az.ref(refId) in the same context to rehydrate it or az.peek(value) for a bounded shape summary.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "contextId": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}$"
        },
        "code": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 262144
        },
        "timeoutMs": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 3600000,
          "default": 60000
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "contextId",
        "code"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"
    },
    "outputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "value": {},
        "console": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "consoleOmitted": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "calls": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "callsOmitted": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "context": {
          "type": "object"
        },
        "sensitivity": {
          "enum": [
            "public",
            "customerData",
            "secret"
          ]
        },
        "correlationId": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "value",
        "console",
        "consoleOmitted",
        "calls",
        "callsOmitted",
        "context",
        "sensitivity",
        "correlationId"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": true
    }
  },
  {
